func=jag::Packet::g4Scrambled	func_addr=0x003568b0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Packet::g4Scrambled — mode-selected 4-byte reader. Consumes one mode byte from *(packet+0x28) (advances +1), then reads a uint32 whose byte order depends on the mode:\n  0 \e gT_unsigned_int  -> plain big-endian   (server: writeInt / p4)\n  1 \e g4_alt1          -> little-endian      (server: writeIntLittle / p4_alt1)\n  2 \e g4_alt2          -> middle-endian      (server: writeIntMiddle / p4_alt2)\n  3 \e g4_alt3          -> inverse-middle     (server: writeIntInverseMiddle / p4_alt3)\nUsed for the 32-bit hitmark DAMAGE field in the WIDE hits blocks (player bit25, npc bit32).
