func=jag::ClientCrashReportingDataProvider::GetAddress	func_addr=0x00339f30	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=291	cu_index_from_entry=68	text=Project X patcher target: a SECOND occurrence of the live-mode HTTP content port literal in this build. The compiler inlined the entire body of jag::WorldLobbyData::GetHTTPURL here, so this is the same logic as that standalone function rather than a distinct one.\n\nUsed when the ClientParameters TLS flag is clear and the server profile is the live/default one; the runtime patcher must rewrite this immediate with the port from PROJECTX_HTTP_PORT here as well.\n\nHow the patcher locates it: by the pair of world-port base constants this block adds to the world id, not by the surrounding opcode bytes. Those bytes differ from the standalone function because this inlined copy is register-allocated differently, so a byte signature written for that site will not match here.\n\nSkipping this site leaves the crash-reporting data provider reporting the unpatched port.
func=jag::Packet::gScrambledArrayBuffer	func_addr=0x00356030	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Packet::gScrambledArrayBuffer — bulk array analog of jag::Packet::gScrambledByte (0x0047f840). Reads ONE transform-selector byte from the cipher cursor at packet+0x28 (post-incremented; points at an in-binary const table, NOT the wire), then copies `length` data bytes from packet+0x10 (pos at +0x18) into dest+0x10 using that mode:\n  mode 0 \e forward, raw           (readFully)\n  mode 1 \e reverse, raw           (readFully, byte-reversed)\n  mode 2 \e forward, byte-0x80     (per-byte readUByteAdd; clean \e wire-128)\n  mode 3 \e reverse, byte-0x80     (per-byte readUByteAdd, byte-reversed)\nUsed by ProcessExtendedInfo for the APPEARANCE payload (cipher table \e APPEARANCE_EXTINFO_SCRAMBLE_CIPHER  \e {0x03,0x02}; entry[1]\e2 -> appearance payload is mode 2). VERIFIED 948-5 against authentic live PLAYER_INFO capture (payload bytes are clean+0x80 on the wire).
