func=jag::ClientProt::SendMapBuildComplete	func_addr=0x00252100	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ClientProt MAP_BUILD_COMPLETE emitter. Uses descriptor jag::ClientProt  (registered in ClientProt::RegisterAll  via the ClientProt ctor with opcode\e0x6B(107), size\e0). Descriptor layout: +0x0 opcode\e0x6B, +0x4 size\e0. FUN_00136920 builds a TcpConnectionMessage from (descriptor->opcode, descriptor->size, netbuf); size 0 \e> bare opcode byte, NO payload (the on-wire opcode is then ISAAC-enciphered; server sees 107 pre-cipher). After sending, this drains/finalizes every pending per-map-square build (FUN_002b3990 over the build hashmap at param_1+0xf8) and clears the build queue (param_1+0x158). This is the terminal scene/map-build-complete step. Sole caller: FUN_002def20 (build-complete state handler). A stalled/partial scene build never reaches this -> op107 never emitted.
