func=jag::PacketHandlers::VorbisPreloadSounds	func_addr=0x00122720	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eVORBIS_PRELOAD_SOUNDS direction\eSERVER opcode\e194 size\e4\n\nPayload: g4_alt3 sound group id (inverse-middle-endian int).\nGuarded on the audio system (Client+0x195b8) being initialised and the id being non-negative, it\ncalls FUN_007abdc0(audioMgr, id, 1) -- the get-or-create for a cached vorbis sound resource, keyed\nby (id << 1) | kind -- and then invokes vftable+0x10 on the resulting resource. It never starts\nplayback and never touches a mixer channel.\nEvidence: FUN_007abdc0 has exactly two callers -- this handler and FUN_00aee950, which is the\nplayback routine the confirmed VORBIS_SOUND_GROUP  uses. Taking the same resource\nloader without the playback path is a preload.
