func=jag::ClientProt::SendDisplayInfo	func_addr=0x001a2cf0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::SendDisplayInfo — the REAL window/canvas-dimensions packet ("WINDOW_STATUS"). 949: descriptor 0x01684240, RegisterAll ClientProt(0x01684240, id\e0x30, size\e6) \e> ClientProt op48 (0x30), FIXED 6 bytes. Wire: [op48][p1 displayMode: 2\eresizable / 3\efocused-fullscreen-subwindow][p2 width (BE)][p2 height (BE)][p1 flag \e client+0x140 (antialias)]. Width/height read from the display/canvas object DAT_01692e98+0x1b8 (FUN_00aacac0\ewidth, FUN_00aaca90\eheight). Sent via ConnectionManager::GetActiveConnection; in lobby->world it is the FIRST ClientProt on the new world socket (before op98 + REBUILD_NORMAL) and again on any resize. NOTE: op48 in 949 (was op52 in 948-5). The server's op114\eWINDOW_STATUS stub is WRONG — op114 is chat filter; window/canvas dims are THIS op48.
