func=jag::Packet::gScrambledShort	func_addr=0x00356af0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Packet::gScrambledShort - scrambled 2-byte reader. Body byte-identical to gScrambledUshort . Consumes ONE mode-selector byte from the in-binary cipher table via the cursor at packet+0x28 (post-incremented; NOT from the wire), then reads 2 bytes with that transform:\n  mode 0 -> BE  (b0<<8 | b1)                \e readUShort  (g2)\n  mode 1 -> LE  (b1<<8 | b0)                \e readUShortLittle (g2LE)\n  mode 2 -> BE, low byte +0x80              \e readUShortAdd  (g2_add)\n  mode 3 -> LE, low byte +0x80              \e readUShortAddLittle (g2_add_LE)\nUsed throughout PlayerEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo and NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfoNPC for scrambled u16 fields. (signed/unsigned inferred \e signed sibling of gScrambledUshort; does not affect wire bytes.) VERIFIED 948-5.
