func=jag::LoginManager::LoginStepWaitingServerClientVar	func_addr=0x001985c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=LoginStepWaitingServerClientVar (login state 0x10e\e270) — PARSES the server-perm VarClient (varc) block (TASK B "Part A"). NOTE: Jagex's beta symbol for this 0x10e handler is actually "LoginStepWaitingServerClientVarConfigData"; the 0x104 reader is Jagex's "LoginStepWaitingServerClientVar" — the two suffixes are SWAPPED in this DB vs the real symbols (kept as-is to match project login-protocol.md).\n\nBlock source \e Packet @ loginMgr+0x198 (size@+0x1a0, data@+0x1a8, pos@+0x1b0). Format:\n  byte[0] \e continuationFlag (read once: cVar6). 1 \e> this is the final block, send LoginProt continue + go state 0x82; 0 \e> more [len][block] follow, go back to state 0xfa.\n  position starts at 1 (skips the flag byte). Then repeat while pos < blockSize:\n    [g2 id]  \e big-endian u16 var id (read direct: *(u16*)(block+pos), bswap16; pos+\e2)\n    [value]  \e decoded by the var's ScriptVarType codec: lookup VarType by id in VarTypeList (vtable+0x40), then (*(ScriptVarType_vtable+0x18))(codec, &VarValue, packet@loginMgr+0x198). The packet position (loginMgr+0x1b0) is advanced by the codec.\n    Then ConfigProvider::GetVarType(cp, DAT_013a3a40 \e VarDomainType::CLIENT, id) resolves the varc and SetVarValue stores it into the client var domain (lVar3+0x73a8).\n  If DecodeVarValue returns the not-found sentinel, parsing aborts.\nValue encoding per ScriptVarType (verified in beta librs2client.so jag::game::BaseVarType*::Decode; target codecs unnamed): INTEGER\eg4 (4B BE); LONG\eg8 (8B BE); STRING\enull-terminated CP1252 (empty\esingle 0x00); COORDFINE\eg1 level + g4 x + g4 y + g4 z (13B). Type is NOT on the wire; both ends derive it from the var's cache definition.
