func=jag::packethandlers::PlayerInfo::PLAYER_INFO_DECODE_2	func_addr=0x001bbfa0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=HYPOTHESIS / MISLABELED: despite the symbol name 'PLAYER_INFO_DECODE_2', this is NOT the per-tick PLAYER_INFO (op22 GPI) decoder. The real GPI handler is jag::PacketHandlers::PlayerInfo . This function reads two CP1252->UTF8 strings + gT_unsigned_int + gT_unsigned_short, builds an FNV-hashed name table, emits a localized "%s%d%s matches, %s%d sent" message, and is reached from ConsoleFeedback (). Likely a name-search / console-feedback / autocomplete results decoder (a different ServerProt). Do NOT treat as GPI; do NOT trust the current name. Needs its own RE pass + opcode binding before renaming.
func=jag::opcode::oc_paramvalue	func_addr=0x0033db80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::opcode::oc_paramvalue — CS2 ObjType param value accessor (implicit-obj-context version). Pops 1 int from stack (param ID). Reads the active ObjType context from the script state at +0xbfe0 (if flag at +0x20 set) or +0xbfc0 (else). Looks up ParamType via ParamType::GetById equivalent. Then performs binary search through the obj's param list (puVar5[1] + 0x128, stride 0x28). Differentiates string vs int by comparing the ParamType's tag at +0x38 against the string-type marker: - String params: push value onto string stack (+0x10a8). - Int params: push via int stack (+0x100). Default value from ParamType +0x40 if no match found. Differs from item_getparam/mec_param which pop 2 ints (obj + param) — this uses the implicit active-obj context.
