func=jag::ClientProt::PopEventMouseMoveSample	func_addr=0x0017b1a0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::PopEventMouseMoveSample -- vtable slot 4. Pops the oldest movement sample and\nadvances MouseInputRecorder::moveRingRead, or returns NULL when the ring is empty. Reaches the\nrecorder through sender->client -> MainLogicManager -> its MouseInputRecorder sub-object.\n\nThe read cursor is advanced for EVERY pop, including samples the caller then discards under the\nsame-position elision rule, so an elided sample is still consumed.\n\nProof of the two-ring layout: MainLogicManager's MouseInputRecorder holds a 50-slot press ring\nfollowed by its cursor pair, then a 200-slot movement ring followed by ITS cursor pair. Confirmed\nthree ways: this pop, the two init loops in jag::MainLogicManager::Construct (each followed by an\n8-byte store clearing exactly that ring's cursor pair), and jag::Client::DiscardPendingInput,\nwhich drains both rings by copying write into read.
