func=jag::ClientProt::EventMouseProtHasPendingWork	func_addr=0x0017b210	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::EventMouseProtHasPendingWork -- vtable slot 0 of the event mouse prot sender,\nand the FULL emission predicate for the movement-history stage.\n\nReturns true when EITHER\n  (a) the recorder's CLICK ring is non-empty (write !\e read), or\n  (b) (global clock - sender->lastMoveSampleTime) > the staleness interval.\nNote (a): a pending CLICK forces the movement-history packet out in the same tick, and the pump\nemits the history packet BEFORE the click packet. Note (b): the reference is the last movement\nsample actually WRITTEN to a packet, not the last tick, so a long run of elided same-position\nsamples still lets the timer expire and fire an (almost empty) packet. Note that the movement\nring's own emptiness is NOT part of this predicate: the stage can be entered with nothing to pop,\nin which case it allocates no packet and falls through.\n\nWhen this returns false the driver SKIPS the whole history stage but still tail-calls slot 1\n(the click sender) unconditionally; the click sender self-guards on its own ring.
