func=eastl::rbtree::next	func_addr=0x00c84790	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=eastl::rbtree::next — standard EASTL/STL red-black tree successor iteration. Node layout (offsets in bytes): +0x00 pointer to left child, +0x08 pointer to right child (NEXT in iteration order), +0x10 pointer to parent. Node payload starts after +0x18 (varies by node type). Algorithm: if node has a right child (+0x08 !\e null), descend to its leftmost node and return it; otherwise walk up via parent (+0x10) until arriving from a left child (came-from-right keeps walking up), returning that parent (or the node itself if the root is hit). Used heavily to iterate static-location / world trees with a sentinel node.
func=jag::game::LinkMap::ReadTileFlags	func_addr=0x00589cc0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Reads the per-tile MAPS/TILES "settings" byte (cache flags&0x2 field) from the composite grid subcontainer+0x1f0. This byte \e\e the raw cache settings byte. CLIENT-CONFIRMED bit meanings (see enum MapTileSettingsFlag): 0x1\eCLIPPED/blocked-floor (read by engine collision from cache tileFlags; client itself does not test it here), 0x2\eBRIDGE/link-below (HasBridgeFlag; entities shifted down one level), 0x4\eUNDER_ROOF (GetUnderRoofFlag), 0x8\eFORCE_LOWEST_LEVEL/level-link (IsOnCorrectLevel). Bits 0x10/0x20/0x40/0x80 are NOT tested by any client consumer of this byte (searched all callers of ReadTileFlags/ReadTileByte3D). WATER is NOT a bit in this byte: the client is not a pathfinder and reads no water flag; rendered water \e separate MAPS "WATER_TILES" file (group 4) -> WaterPatch/WaterType mesh patches. The 2nd per-tile grid at subcontainer+0x258 (reader FUN_00501950) is the minimap map-scene id, not water.
