func=jag::input::TouchLongPressToRightClick	func_addr=0x00c93220	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=TOUCH-ONLY long-press -> right-click emulation. WARNING: `this` is NOT a jag::input::Input. It is the touch tracker (owning class name unidentified in this build; HYPOTHESIS only): +0x48 \e Input*, +0x50 \e touch-point map, +0x58 \e touch array, +0x68 \e touch count, +0x430 \e active touch id, +0x438 \e suppress flag, +0x440 \e press timestamp (ms), +0x44d/+0x44e/+0x44f \e state flags. Its vtable is at 0x01416cd0.\nBecause a jag::input::Input is only 0xA0 bytes, calling this with an Input* reads out-of-object memory at +0x44f/+0x68 and will silently no-op or fault. There is NO native synthetic-right-click helper in this binary; to synthesise a right click, reproduce what the SDL pump does for SDL_BUTTON_RIGHT: set InputState.rightButtonDown then CallListeners_ff(packedXY, globalHandler+0x108) / +0x148.
