func=jag::PlayerEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c960	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=379	cu_index_from_entry=78	text=FACE_DIRECTION (player ext-info bit7) — one-shot angle facing. 1x gScrambledShort (selector 0xd66d96 \e mode3 \e g2_add_LE) -> JagexAngleToRadians -> render-angle float at player+0x23c. Server: writeShortAddLittle(angle), 0..16383, full circle 16384. Re-send each tick to track a moving target. This is the player's only facing flag that the 949-1 client actually APPLIES.\n\nCORRECTION (was 'face-entity absent'): the player ext-info wire DOES carry a FACE/INTERACT-ENTITY index at bit 8 (mask 0x100, dispatch #19) as p1,p1,gScrambledShort(g2LE index) — CONFIRMED by live capture. See the bit-8 body . BUT that 949-1 handler READS and DISCARDS it (no store), so the local client applies facing via prediction, not via bit 8. My earlier grep-based 'no store/DecRef' finding was about the client NOT applying it; it did not mean the wire flag was absent — it isn't.
func=jag::PlayerEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c960	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=416	cu_index_from_entry=86	text=PLAYER HITS NARROW block (mask bit4 / 0x10). Mode table @PlayerHitsNarrowModeTable(0xd66d7a)\e{00 01 00 01 01 02 01}. Legacy small-damage channel (damage \e smart, max 0x7ffd). NOT the live player channel (players use bit25 wide).\nWIRE:\n  hitmarkCount : gScrambledByte mode0\ePLAIN\n  per hitmark: type\egSmart1or2 ; damage\egSmart1or2 [0x7ffe: soak byte gScrambledByte mode1\eADD ; 0x7fff: type2,damage,soak,extra all gSmart1or2] ; delay\egSmart1or2\n  headbarCount : gScrambledByte mode0\ePLAIN\n  per headbar: type/sel/duration\egSmart1or2 ; front\egScrambledByte mode1\eADD ; [twoFill]back(bar1)\eADD ; transId\egSmart1or2Minus1 ; [transId>\e0] front2\egScrambledByte mode2\eINVERSE, [twoFill]back2\egScrambledByte mode1\eADD
func=jag::PlayerEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c960	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=505	cu_index_from_entry=106	text=ANIMATION / seq (player ext-info bit1). NOT exact-move (that is bit6 SetForcedMovement). Reads 4x gSmart2or4s (BE big-smart anim-layer ids; 2-byte form 0x7fff \e -1 \e empty layer, else 4-byte when hi bit set) then 1 gScrambledByte delay/speed, selector  \e mode 0 \e raw g1. Dispatches vtable+0x1e0 (RequestAnimation; concrete FUN_000f24f0/FUN_00aef220) which looks up each id as a SeqType and takes its duration (+0xa48). Server encode: 4x writeBigSmart(layerId, empty\e0x7fff) + writeByte(delay). CONFIRMED 949-1. (Corrects prior EXACT_MOVE label on bit1.)
func=jag::PlayerEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c960	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=2745	cu_index_from_entry=544	text=PLAYER HITS WIDE block (mask bit25 / 0x2000000). Mode table @PlayerHitsWideModeTable(0xd66d38)\e{01 03 01 03 01 01 03}. THE live-combat channel for players (32-bit damage).\nWIRE (read order):\n  hitmarkCount : gScrambledByte mode1\eADD           (server writeByteAdd)\n  per hitmark:\n    type       : gSmart1or2                          (writeSmart; 0x7fff/0x7ffe \e special forms)\n    damage     : g4Scrambled mode3\einverse-middle    (writeIntInverseMiddle)   [0x7ffe form: soak byte via gScrambledByte mode3\eSUBTRACT]\n    [0x7fff big form only: after type2(smart) -> damage\eg4Scrambled mode3, soak\esmart, extra\eg4Scrambled mode1\eLE]\n    delay      : gSmart1or2                           (writeSmart)\n  headbarCount : gScrambledByte mode1\eADD            (writeByteAdd)\n  per headbar:\n    type       : gSmart1or2 ; sel\egSmart1or2 (0x7fff\eremove)\n    duration   : gSmart1or2\n    front      : gScrambledByte mode3\eSUBTRACT\n    [sel!\e0 twoFill] back(bar1): gScrambledByte mode1\eADD\n    transId    : gSmart1or2Minus1 (writeSmart(id+1))\n    [transId>\e0] front2: gScrambledByte mode1\eADD ; [twoFill] back2: gScrambledByte mode3\eSUBTRACT\nNOT byte-identical to NPC bit32: count\eADD (npc PLAIN), headbarCount\eADD (npc INVERSE), extra\eLE (npc MIDDLE), back/front2\eADD (npc PLAIN), back2\eSUBTRACT (npc INVERSE).
func=jag::PlayerEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c960	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=8924	cu_index_from_entry=1750	text=PLAYER_INFO ext-info bit8 (mask 0x100) \e FACE_ENTITY, out-of-line body (jumped from 0x166318). Reads 3 fields via the block transform selector : gScrambledByte, gScrambledByte, gScrambledShort(index) -> wire p1(a) p1(b) writeShortLittle(index); captured constant a\e0x04 b\e0x01, index\eg2LE (raw idx for NPC <0x8000, 0x8000|playerIdx for player). VERIFIED (asm): all three return values are DISCARDED - no store to +0x10d0/+0x1B4/+0x23c, no resolve call, then JMP back. The 949-1 client READS AND IGNORES player FACE_ENTITY; it does NOT orient the model. Contrast NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo bit10 which DOES store +0x10d0. Server-driven player facing must instead use bit7 FACE_DIRECTION (angle -> +0x23c).
func=jag::PlayerEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c960	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=9672	cu_index_from_entry=1908	text=FACE_DIRECTION (player bit7) store: JagexAngleToRadians(short) -> render-angle float at player+0x23c. Wire \e writeShortAddLittle(angle), angle in 0..16383 (full circle 16384). Server: angle \e round(atan2(-dx,-dy)*2607.5945876) & 0x3FFF where dx\eeast delta, dy\enorth delta; compass S\e0,W\e4096,N\e8192,E\e12288.
func=jag::ClientProt::SendMessagePrivate	func_addr=0x003266c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::SendMessagePrivate — XTEA-encrypted PM VARIANT. Descriptor 0x01684020, registered id 82 size -2 \e> ClientProt op82 (var_short). Consumes 3 CS2 strings + 2 CS2 ints. Wire: [op82][size:u16][pStr A][pStr B][p1 C][p1 (D\e\e1) bool][pStr E (message)][+7 pad][Packet::tinyKeyEncrypt over the body]. IMPORTANT: this is NOT the free-text PM the retail client emits — live capture shows the user's free-text PM (lobby AND in-world) is op71 (jag::opcode::ChatSendPrivate / CHAT_SENDPRIVATE, Huffman body, no XTEA). op82 is a distinct encrypted 3-string message variant, not observed in captured PM flows. The server's op82\eMESSAGE_PRIVATE label is misplaced: MESSAGE_PRIVATE belongs on op71.
