func=jag::packethandlers::Social::op130_RELATIONSHIP_DELTA_UNCONFIRMED	func_addr=0x001e6b30	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt op130 (0x82), VarByte. IDENTITY UNCONFIRMED — do NOT trust the "UPDATE_IGNORELIST" name in any prior label/CSV.\n\nThis is NOT the rev-947 UPDATE_IGNORELIST (a loop of {flag-byte + 3 CP1252 strings} ignore records). Decompile shows a SINGLE relationship/friend entry built from a 64-bit flag mask:\n  - gT_ulong flagMask\n  - if mask\e\e0: clears all fields (a remove/empty-entry form)\n  - else ~48 conditionally-gated fields keyed by individual mask bits 0..0x2f (smart readers, coord triples, packed-uint->3 floats color/vector, trailing g2)\n  - allocates a 0x1e0-byte entry, stores to *(RelationshipManager+0x98), frees old, sets dirty flag +0xa0 \e 1.\n\nPer-friend RELATIONSHIP DELTA packet (single entry, flag-gated), redesigned in 948. CRITICAL: needs a live lobby capture with a friended/ignored account to nail the flag-bit -> field mapping. LEAVE AS UNKNOWN until then.
