func=jag::MainLogicManager::KeyboardInputRecorder::OnKeyChar	func_addr=0x00caf840	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::MainLogicManager::KeyboardInputRecorder::OnKeyChar -- producer of the SECOND keyboard ring,\nthe typed-character ring. Pushes a KeyEvent of the identical record type as the key ring but with\nkeyId \e -1, rawKeyCode \e -1, charCode \e the typed character, repeat \e 0 and modifierMask reduced\nto its low three bits. Same 255-slot, drop-oldest wrap rule as the key ring, with its own cursor\npair immediately after the array.\n\nThe two rings are laid out back to back with homogeneous records, which is what makes it possible\nfor a downstream stage to merge them into a single per-tick list.\n\nOPEN QUESTION (do not assume): whether typed characters reach the server at all. The\nserver-bound key stage writes only the LOW BYTE of keyId per record and filters on repeat being\nclear; a char record would satisfy that filter and would serialise as 0xFF. Either the stage's\nsource list excludes char records, or char records are what the 0xFF-keyed entries are. Not\nresolved in this pass -- confirm by capture before building a producer for it.\n\nName provenance: descriptive project coinage. The engine's existing OnKeyCharInner capture hook\nsits upstream of this delegate.
