func=jag::LoginManager::StartWorldLogin	func_addr=0x001b7b80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::LoginManager::StartWorldLogin - begins the WORLD login (loginType\e2). Pulls the game-connection ClientStream shared_ptr from ConnectionManager+0x10/+0x18 (the GAME slot, distinct from the lobby/login slot at CM+0x28), reuses the lobby-login credentials/token strings at LoginMgr+0x70/+0x88, then calls StartLogin(type\e2,...). StartLogin -> login sub-state 10 -> LoginStepWaitingConnectionOpened opens a NEW socket to WorldSwitcher+0x20 (committed world target) host:port, then runs the standard NXT login handshake (CreateLoginRSAPacket: RSA-wrapped block) over that fresh socket. Triggered by (a) OnMainStateTransition on state 0x25 (set by SWITCH_WORLD op213), or (b) the lobby 'play' CS2 opcode FUN_002dc380 once the world target is already committed. RE rs2client.948-5.
func=jag::game::CombinedLocationSection::MeshTrianglePickTest	func_addr=0x004e1d80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=CombinedLocationSection mesh pick test (slot 0xa0 of vftable 0x01425520), the structural analogue of the Location pick test at 0x00481e70.\n\nEstablishes how a CombinedLocationSection reaches its renderable, and it is NOT through a render-node member of its own: the chain is section+0x08 (the GraphNode) -> +0x130 -> +0x1a0 (the attached entity) -> +0xf8 (the render model). Only after that third hop do the ORenderModel accesses appear - world transform at +0x30 and the mesh-component vector dereferenced off +0x268 - which is exactly the shape the Location pick test reaches directly off Location's own render-node slot.\n\nConsequence for the engine offset tables: a CombinedLocationSection render-node FIELD does not exist. The complete-object destructor (0x004b95f0) enumerates every refcounted member of the class and lists only +0xa8, +0x68, +0x58, +0x48 and +0x08, and sizeof is 0x110 - so the values the tables shipped for OCombinedLocationSection.RENDER_NODE / RENDER_NODE_CTRL / PARENT_COMBINED_LOCATION all fall past the end of the object and read whatever the pool allocator left there. They were copied from jag::game::Location, whose layout is unrelated to this class. Those three keys are withheld from the generated tables until someone models the GraphNode hop instead; withheld makes the engine throw, whereas the copied values silently returned garbage pointers.
