func=jag::LoginManager::LoginStepWaitingConnectionOpened	func_addr=0x0018af50	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::LoginManager::LoginStepWaitingConnectionOpened - the world/lobby RECONNECT step (login sub-state 0xe). Reads WorldSwitcher (client+RELA[0xd01]); for loginType (LoginMgr+0x20)\e\e2 (WORLD) target\e*(WS+0x20), else (LOBBY) target\e*(WS+0x30). port \e (target+0x2c\e\e0) ? port1(target+0x28) : port2(target+0x2a). Calls game::ServerConnection::OpenConnection(conn, target+0x10 /*host string*/, port) which builds a fresh ClientStream to \\"host:port\\". PROOF that lobby<->world is a RECONNECT to the world's own host:port (separate socket), NOT socket reuse. The world and lobby can be separate servers on separate ports. RE rs2client.948-5.
