func=jag::Js5ResourceProvider::RequestGroupFromDisk	func_addr=0x00b62190	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=CRASH SITE for JS5 startup SIGSEGV (fault PC \e 0xb61ad0). Reftable/index path: groupId\e\e0xffffffff.\nthis+0x25b8 \e Js5MasterIndex* (built in WorkerOnMessage case 10). Trap at 0xb61ad0 when masterIndex->archive_count(+0x10) <\e archiveId.\nROOT CAUSE (refined): the master index was REJECTED by the ctor (Js5MasterIndex ) - RSA-decrypted length !\e 65 OR whirlpool(body) !\e plaintext[1..64] - so archive_count is left 0 while the object is still stored non-null at this+0x25b8. The first low-index reftable request (e.g. archiveId\e2) then trips 0 <\e 2 -> UD2. (NOT a too-small archive-count byte, and NOT the RSA block magic byte, which is never checked.) Fix: RSA key patch must match the signer; whirlpool must cover packetData[5..endOfEntries].
