func=jag::Client::FUN_000c04a0	func_addr=0x000b3880	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=4401	cu_index_from_entry=560	text=SDL EVENT PUMP - the ONLY place SDL touches input in this binary. Everything below jag::input::Input is platform independent; the Windows build feeds the same virtuals from its WndProc and the macOS build from NSEvent, so this pump is the Linux-only adapter.\nTranslation table (SDL_Event.type -> Input entry):\n  0x300 SDL_KEYDOWN        -> vtable+0x10 OnKeyDown(keysym.sym); if keysym.scancode\e\e0x35 (GRAVE) also fires OnKeyDown(0x1ca3) FIRST\n  0x301 SDL_KEYUP          -> vtable+0x18 OnKeyUp(keysym.sym); same 0x1ca3 pre-fire\n  0x303 SDL_TEXTINPUT      -> UTF-8 decode of event.text.text -> vtable+0x20 OnKeyChar(codepoint)\n  0x400 SDL_MOUSEMOTION    -> OnMouseMotion((float)event.motion.x, (float)event.motion.y)\n  0x401 SDL_MOUSEBUTTONDOWN-> btn1 OnLeftButtonDown | btn2 InputState.middleButtonDown\e1 + CallListeners(handler+0x88) | btn3 rightButtonDown\e1 + CallListeners(handler+0x108) | btn4/5 OnScrollWheel(0,0)\n  0x402 SDL_MOUSEBUTTONUP  -> btn1 OnLeftButtonUp  | btn2 middleButtonDown\e0 + CallListeners(handler+0xC8) | btn3 rightButtonDown\e0 + CallListeners(handler+0x148)\n  0x403 SDL_MOUSEWHEEL     -> OnScrollWheel((float)wheel.x, (float)wheel.y)\n  0x600 SDL_JOYAXISMOTION  -> gamepad axis global + handler+0x448; axis>4 also handler+0x488 (trigger, value>>7)\n  0x603/4 SDL_JOYBUTTON*   -> gamepad button global + handler+0x408\n  0x100 SDL_QUIT           -> Client vtable+0x50\nDispatch is SYNCHRONOUS on this thread - there is no intermediate event queue between SDL and jag::input::Input. Once SDL_PollEvent drains, Client vtable+0x38 runs the frame. Any injected input must therefore be delivered on THIS thread to match the real ordering.
func=jag::Client::FUN_000c04a0	func_addr=0x000b3880	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=8139	cu_index_from_entry=1388	text=SDL_MOUSEBUTTONDOWN button 2 (middle). Linux has NO jag::input::Input::OnMiddleButtonDown - the pump writes g_middleButtonState inline and calls EventListeners::CallListeners_ff on globalHandler->onMMouseDown directly. Same for button 3 (right). Only button 1 goes through a named Input method.
