func=jag::game::PathingEntity::GetFaceEntityIndex	func_addr=0x0048e070	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Per-frame model face/lock-on target resolver (installed as a callback; INDIRECTION xrefs). Returns the entity index this model orients toward, in priority order: (1) entity+0x10d0 \e server-forced FACE_ENTITY lock (set by NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo bit10 store  / stop ; players\e0x8000|playerIdx, npcs\eraw idx, -1\enone); (2) entity+0xf38; (3) route/interaction sub-node +0x3d8 (client-predicted target). NOTE: this reads +0x10d0, NOT the client interaction field +0x1B4 (engine OPathingEntity.INTERACTING_NPC_SID). +0x1B4 is a separate field (ctor-init -1 @jag::game PathingEntity ctor 0x4dd5d0) and does NOT drive model facing.
