func=jag::ClientProt::SendQueuedEvents	func_addr=0x0018f380	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::SendQueuedEvents \e\e emitter of ClientProt STORE_SERVERPERM_VARCS (op105, varShort, ProtEntry DAT_01683eb0; RegisterAll index 0x69 size -2). CONFIRMED (prior 'EVENT_NATIVE/UI event stream' hypothesis was WRONG). Flushes the map of CHANGED serverpermanent var_client values (param_1+0x78 hashmap merged into the +0xa8 vector of 0x28-byte {int key, typed value, byte typeTag} records), throttled ~1/sec (param_1+0xa0 +\e 1000ms), capped 0x5dd\e1501B/packet, resumes across packets via index param_1+0xc0. Server replies op200 StoreServerpermVarcsAck (1:1). Payload after varShort len:\n  [0] u8 completeFlag: 1 \e all remaining records fit in this packet (final chunk); 0 \e 1501B cap hit, more follow in the next op105.\n  then repeated per record: pT<short> varcId (2B BE) ; value encoded by the varc's value-domain (int domain \e pT<int> 4B BE; long/string domains would differ - none seen).\n  No count, no terminator; records run to end of payload.\nVERIFIED vs 2 live bodies: 01 |1b35\e1 |0b67\e.. |0b68\e.. |0d89\e.. -> varcIds 6965/2919/2920/3465 (all toplevel_v2 *_savestate_* / *_serverperm). Emitter called from ConnectionManager::LoginProtocolHandler.
