func=jag::Js5ResourceProvider::WorkerOnMessage	func_addr=0x00b70fb0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Js5 worker message dispatch. case 10 \e accept master index (255/255) -> builds this->masterIndex (this+0x25b8) whose archive_count gates all reftable requests. case 0x14 \e deliver index/reftable to disk cache. case 0x1e \e provide group. case 0x28 \e compare/verify master index.\nARCHIVE CAPACITY \e 67 (hardcoded): case 10 zeroes 0x43\e67 per-archive state entries (this+0x25d0); per-archive Js5Index arrays at this+0x26e0/+0x6bf8/+0xb110 are each 67*0x108 (ending at this+0xf628). archiveId directly indexes these 67-slot arrays (no per-array bound), so requestable archiveId is 0..66. Therefore master-index archive_count byte MUST be >\e 67 to avoid the RequestGroupFromDisk/SendIndex assert (archiveId < archive_count).
func=jag::Js5ResourceProvider::WorkerOnMessage	func_addr=0x00b70fb0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=1146	cu_index_from_entry=217	text=case 10 (accept master index 255/255): parse received blob into a Js5MasterIndex (alloc 0x20) and store at this+0x25b8. Js5MasterIndex.archive_count(+0x10) \e the single archive-count byte in the blob. THIS is the value RequestGroupFromDisk / SendIndex bounds-check archiveId against. Later in this case the per-archive disk group-status array (diskCache+0x10198+archiveId*0x20) is (re)sized to masterIndexEntry.file_count+1.
