func=jag::game::Conversion::JagexAngleToRadians	func_addr=0x00a8b370	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=JagexAngle -> radians. Full circle \e 16384 units (0x4000): value & 0x3FFF, values > 0x2000 wrapped by subtracting 16384.0 (DAT_00d677a4) to signed [-8192,8192), then * (2*PI/16384) \e pi/8192 (DAT_010bf1e0 \e 0x39C90FDB). NOT 2048 and NOT 65536. FACE_DIRECTION (player bit7) feeds the full 16-bit short here and stores the float at player+0x23c.
func=jag::callstack::capture_stack_back_trace	func_addr=0x00d74a60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::callstack::capture_stack_back_trace - libgcc/EH stack unwinder loop. Walks the current stack and invokes per-frame callback param_1 (FUN_00a87e50) which appends each return address to the caller's buffer (max 100 frames). Used by FatalSignalHandler to capture the crash backtrace that ReportError later relocates (dladdr vs g_dladdrBaseAnchor) and POSTs to nxtclienterror.ws. The backtrace addresses in the report are module-relative offsets - see MASKING note in ReportError.
