func=jag::game::PathingEntity::SetFinePosition	func_addr=0x004cc350	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=SetFinePosition(this, const float pos[3], bool immediate).\nWrites the entity's LIVE fine position, axis order {X, Z(height), Y}:\n  this+0x270 \e float xFine   this+0x274 \e float height   this+0x278 \e float yFine\nHeight is resampled from the terrain, not taken from pos[1].\nAlso seeds the render smoothing block: 0x280 startNs, 0x288/0x290/0x298 from(x,z,y) as double,\n0x2a0 endNs, 0x2a8/0x2b0/0x2b8 target(x,z,y) as double.\nReads this+0x2c0 (>0 \e> moving) to pick seq field +0xa60 vs +0xa64.
func=jag::game::ClientError::ReportFatalError	func_addr=0x00ca6aa0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::ClientError fatal-error reporter. Builds a human message ("Fatal error occured!" + optional prefix/JagException text from param_5), then if the GLOBAL reporter DAT_015beb98 has the default vtable (FUN_0047d5b0) and a live reporter object (DAT_015beb98[0x116] \e\e client+0x8b0), calls jag::game::ClientError::ReportError (FUN_006ef050) with flags\e7 to POST to nxtclienterror.ws. This is the C++ fatal/exception funnel (distinct from the OS-signal path). DAT_015beb98[0x116]*8 \e\e 0x8b0 \e\e the reporter sub-object offset. Hooking ReportError (0x006ef050) covers this path too.
