func=jag::ClientProt::SendMessagePublicWithEffects	func_addr=0x0032dab0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ClientProt emitter for opcode 87 (0x57), size -1/varByte. Binds to the opcode-87 ClientProt entry; writes a trailing single-byte length (varByte). Parses chat-effect tags (color/wave/etc.) from the message text. NOTE: iEasyScript CSV mis-mapped this to opcode 88; opcode 88 is SendDataReport. MESSAGE_PUBLIC_EFFECTS \e opcode 87.
func=jag::game::World::World	func_addr=0x005df9e0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::World::World(this, sceneManager, RT7Core, Js5ResourceProvider, ConfigProvider, PlayerVarDomain, AssetBuilder, worldArea<WorldAreaType>&, BuildMode(\e3), swMapSquareX(p10), swMapSquareY(p11), neMapSquareX(p12), neMapSquareY(p13), levelHeightGrid&).\nStores the two map-square CORNERS: this+0x13fb4\eswMapSquareX, +0x13fb8\eswMapSquareY, +0x13fbc\eneMapSquareX, +0x13fc0\eneMapSquareY (plane/level count\e3 at +0xa4118).\nThen width \e neX-swX (this+0x13ff0), height \e neY-swY (this+0x13ff4), maxDim (this+0x13ff8), and allocates the World's 2D map-square cell grid (this+0x2800 vector-of-vectors of jag::game::MapSquareStatus) sized (width+1) columns x (height+1) rows.\n\e> the two REBUILD_NORMAL packed coords ARE this World's map-square grid SW & NE corners \e the world area's bounding rectangle / coordinate window (grid origin \e SW corner). Cross-confirmed in librs2client.so jag::game::World::World: stores param_9..param_12 at +0x10e88/+0x10e8c/+0x10e90/+0x10e94 then iVar19\efield_0x10e90-field_0x10e88 (width), iVar29\efield_0x10e94-field_0x10e8c (height) — same logic, offsets drifted.
