func=jag::game::PathingEntity::UpdateHighlight	func_addr=0x00118a00	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::PathingEntity::UpdateHighlight -- writes color/alpha/strength/mode to the entity's render-model at +0x100..+0x134 from the global highlight category table (g_highlightCategoryTable, 8 entries x 16 bytes). Per-category entry layout (verified from _highlight_set_category_* opcode handlers): +0x00 byte mode (0..3); +0x01 byte scale (0..255); +0x04 float R; +0x08 float G; +0x0C float B. Render-model field writes: +0x100 R, +0x104 G, +0x108 B, +0x10c base alpha, +0x110 strength, +0x114 edge alpha, +0x134 silhouette mode. Control paths: (1) combat target -> category 0 directly; (2) category 8 (NO_HIGHLIGHT special), reset to default fade; (3) categories 0..7 -> index into the table. NOTE: engine consumer EntityHighlight.kt writes these render-model slots directly.
func=jag::game::TcpConnectionMessage::Init	func_addr=0x0012f970	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::TcpConnectionMessage::Init -- outgoing form. Constructs a client->server message in\nplace: stores the prot opcode and size, allocates the payload buffer, records the prot back-ptr,\nand emits the ISAAC-enciphered opcode byte.\n\nLayout written (msg): protOpcode u32  (\e *prot), protSize s32  (\e protSize), embedded\njag::Packet  with bufAllocBase  / bufData  / bufWritePos , payloadLength u32\n, prot back-ptr .\n\nBuffer capacity ladder: protSize \e\e -1 -> 0x104; \e\e -2 -> 10000; < 0x13 -> 0x14; < 99 -> 0x62;\nelse 0x104. Allocate into a temp, swap into the message, free the previous buffer if both\npointers were non-null.\n\nOpcode emission: with isaac !\e NULL (outgoing) the first payload byte is\n(opcode + jag::Isaac::TakeNextValue(isaac)) stored straight into the buffer; with isaac \e\e NULL\nit is a plain jag::Packet::pT<unsigned char>. The incoming counterpart passes NULL -- see\njag::game::TcpConnectionMessage::InitIncoming, which ConnectionManager::TcpIn calls.\n\nEvidence: (1) sole caller is the pooled message factory at 0x00136f10, which invokes it as\nInit(msgSlot, *protPtr, *sizePtr, *isaacPtr) -- e.g. from SendEventMouseClick, whose prot\ndescriptor is {u32 opcode, s32 size} at 0x01684520; (2) the Windows program's already-identified\njag::game::TcpConnectionMessage::Init has a byte-identical capacity ladder (same 0x104 / 10000 /\n0x14 / 0x62 constants and the same 0x13 and 99 boundaries), the same field writes, and the same\nallocate/swap/free-old dance; (3) the field offsets match the Windows /jag/net/TcpConnectionMessage\nstruct at 0x0/0x4/0x10/0x18/0x20/0x28, the prot back-ptr differing (0x30 here vs 0x38 there) as\nexpected for a different compiler.
