func=jag::PacketHandlers::ServerTickEnd	func_addr=0x000f3e00	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt op162 (size0). CORRECTED: was mis-deduped as TRIGGER_ONDIALOGABORT. The real TRIGGER_ONDIALOGABORT is op123  (Interfaces; reads the open dialog interface id, checks !\e -1, runs the onDialogAbort hook via FUN_00295f80, matching beta TRIGGER_ONDIALOGABORT \e Interfaces lambda#33 @beta 0x5b38e0 which does InterfaceManager+0x100 !\e -1 -> RunHookLayer). THIS handler instead increments a global counter, calls jag::game::SceneManager::PruneWorlds(), and sets a scene-state flag at SceneManager+0x154 \e 1. It is a scene/world state-reset packet (lives in jag::packethandlers::ClientState alongside DESTROY_ZONE_DATA / RESET_CLIENT_STATE / CLEAR_PENDING_UPDATES). HYPOTHESIS: a size-0 prune-worlds / scene-ready state packet; not matched 1:1 to a single beta-named handler, left as FUN_ pending confirmation. Do NOT rename to TRIGGER_ONDIALOGABORT.
