func=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::UpdateAndRenderHeadbars	func_addr=0x002b73a0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::UpdateAndRenderHeadbars(ctx, PathingEntity* owner)\n\nPer-frame prune + draw of the headbar ring at owner+0xef8 (engine\nOPathingEntity.HITMARKS_AND_HEADBARS), vector at ring+0x28 (engine\nOHitmarksAndHeadbars.HEADBAR_LINKEDLIST_VECTOR_START), 0x1b0-byte slots.\ncurrentCycle \e *(uint*)(*ctx + 0x500).\n\nPer slot, walk the list to the LAST node with startCycle <\e currentCycle (that\nis the active state; later nodes are scheduled for the future). Older nodes\nbefore it are dropped. The active node itself is dropped when\n\n    startCycle + node->transitionCycles + def1[0x4c] < currentCycle\n\nand if that empties the slot, the slot is erased from the vector\n(FUN_00490830). This is the ONLY client-side auto-removal -- it is exactly the\nmoment DrawHeadbar's fade alpha reaches 0, so a bar is never removed while\nstill visible. There is no "remove when full" and no "remove N cycles after\nlast update" rule; a bar with a large def1[0x4c] persists until it expires or\nRemoveHeadbar drops its type.\n\nDraw pass: elapsed \e currentCycle - startCycle; calls DrawHeadbar twice --\n(def1, bar1FromFill, bar1ToFill, transitionCycles, elapsed) and, when def2 is\nnon-null, (def2, bar2FromFill, bar2ToFill, transitionCycles, elapsed).\nBars stack vertically using max(def1[0x40], def2[0x40]) against the ctx+0x78\ny-cursor.
