func=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::AddHitmark	func_addr=0x004c8670	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::AddHitmark. 'type' is a RAW cache hitmark-def id (gameval `hitmark`): looked up via vtable call (plVar1+0x40)(this,type,0) to fetch the HitmarkType (appearance). No masking on type. Record \e 0x18 bytes / 6 ints: [0]\etype [1]\edamage [2]\eendCycle(\ecycle+delay+def[0x44]) [3]\esoak [4]\eextra(2nd number) [5]\edef[0x44]. def[0x80] selects overwrite slot policy (0/1/other). Sentinels 0x7fff/0x7ffe are resolved by the DECODER (wire-form selectors), never reach here as type.
