func=jag::PacketHandlers::NewAudio945	func_addr=0x00121630	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eNEW_AUDIO_945 direction\eSERVER opcode\e210 size\e4\n\nASSIGNED BY ELIMINATION -- lower confidence than the rest of this bucket. The other seven size-4\nhandlers were each positively proven and NEW_AUDIO_945 was the only official name left; the counts\nare equal (8 handlers / 8 names). NEW_AUDIO_945 is itself a placeholder name, so this assignment\ncarries no semantic claim beyond "an audio packet".\n\nPayload: g4 (unsigned int).\nPositively established: the handler runs against the audio system at Client+0x195b8 -- the same\nmanager used by the confirmed VORBIS_SOUND_GROUP  and VORBIS_PRELOAD_SOUNDS\n -- and dispatches vftable+0x38 on the sub-object at audioMgr+0x2950 with\n(ctx\eaudioMgr+0x2960, value, 0, 2, 0). The precise effect was not traced.
func=jag::game::AnimationWrapper::Create	func_addr=0x0075c0d0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=AnimationWrapper factory. Pool-allocates a 0x68-byte control block and publishes the wrapper at ctrl+0x20, so the caller receives {ctrl, obj}. Wrapper layout, identical to the PE Create: +0x00 seq id (copied from animType+0x8), +0x08/+0x10 animation-type shared_ptr, +0x18 playback state, +0x20 flag byte, +0x24 frame cursor seeded to -1, +0x28 per-frame event std::function, +0x40 its invoker.
